# Planner consumer #1 — bare-param mutation in a `while … else:` ELSE body
# (mutated ONLY in the else, so this exercises the loop-else scan extension, not
# the loop body). The else body lowers via `lower_block_scoped`; folding it into
# the pre-LOOP hoist scan (which dominates the else exit) materializes the param
# there. `while … else` is OUT of the ggdef phase-0 subset, so this lives in
# known_gaps/ and is validated on the two production backends only: C=3,4 and
# LLVM=3,4 (pre-fix both printed 4,4). SH note: the SH loop pre-header uses a
# whole-fn suffix scan that already reaches the else body — no divergence.
void f(Vector[int] xs):
    int i = 0
    while i < 1:
        i = i + 1
    else:
        xs.pop()
    print(xs.len())

void main():
    Vector[int] a = [1, 2, 3, 4]
    f(a)
    print(a.len())
